          %hr/
          %blockquote
            %p
              My initial inclination was to call this book
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Music+of+the+Spheres"} The Music of the Spheres
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Ravenel86"} D. Ravenel 86, preface
            %p
              With all due respect to anyone interested in them, the stable homotopy groups of spheres are a mess. (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"}> J. F. Adams 74, p 204
              )
          %hr/
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spheres"} spheres
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n+k}(S^n)
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n+k} \longrightarrow S^n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_{n+k}(S^n) \coloneqq [S^{n+k}, S^n]
                  \\,.
          %p
            For fixed
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            homomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_{n+k}(S^n) \longrightarrow \pi_{n+k+1}(S^{n+1})
          %p
            over all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n+k}(S^n)
            (called the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stem"} stem
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
              of spheres
            (also: the “stable
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stem"} stem
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                    %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_k^S = \coloneqq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_n \pi_{n+k}(S^n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            In fact, by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freudenthal+suspension+theorem"} Freudenthal suspension theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n+k}(S^n)
            stabilizes for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt k+1
            (depend only on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            in this range), whence the name.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
            of sphere are equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+a+spectrum"} homotopy groups of a spectrum
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                    %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_k^S = \pi_k(\mathbb{S})
                  \\,.
          %p
            The stable homotopy groups of spheres are notorious for their immense computational richness. Many of the tools of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            were devised to compute more and more of the stable stems. This notably include the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams-Novikov+spectral+sequence"} Adams-Novikov spectral sequence
          %h2#Tables Tables
          %p
